The element taper is that of the Hy-Gain 205BA 
(not 205CA). Note that the 4.0000" o.d. section 
is modeling the element clamp and boom, and that 
the length of the 1.250" section is shortened by 
the length of the 4.0000" section. The 7/16" 
(0.4375") tips for this design are longer than 
the original tips and will have to be obtained 
locally.

The front-to-rear ratio is better than 20 dB across
the whole band, with an SWR less than 2:1 across
the whole band, and a mid-band free-space gain of 
9.2 dBi. Torque compensator is 2.5" OD PVC, 80.5 " 
long, mounted 12" behind Director 3, on flat metal 
plate with U-bolts. 
